  "text": "How Anthropic, the company behind Claude, lost $80 billion in six months, and why it is about to go public in what would be the biggest IPO ever.\n\nAnthropic made about $16 billion in the first half of 2026 and still reported an $80 billion loss. Most of that loss is an accounting charge that grew because the company got more valuable. The bigger number is the $895 billion it has promised to pay for computers over the next few years. Its own CEO has said that a lab that buys too much compute a year too early can go bankrupt.\n\nOfficial partner: Overnight Studio, the studio behind this channel’s videos. Make your own: madeovernight.com\n\nWould you buy shares in it?\n\n0:00 The $80 billion loss\n0:37 Renting a Brain\n3:29 Too Good\n6:03 Eighty Billion Dollars\n9:10 The Bill\n10:40 Your Turn\n\nFigures as of 4 November 2026, from Anthropic's S-1 filing and reporting by the Wall Street Journal and Reuters.",
