  "text": "Up to 1000x multiplier on stocks & more. Sign up for free with code PAPERB for a chance to win $500! \nLINK: trench.io/?ref=PAPERB\n\nWhy Nvidia is in trouble without Jensen Huang, who resigned as CEO on 12 November 2026, days before the company's earnings report on Tuesday 17 November.\n\nJensen Huang ran Nvidia for 33 years with sixty people reporting straight to him and no number two. He made the bets a finance chief would have refused, like paying for CUDA for years while it earned almost nothing. Now his finance chief, Colette Kress, is interim CEO, and when HP and Intel handed the company to the CFO, both fell behind.\n\nCan Nvidia survive without him?\n\n0:00 Jensen has a huge problem\n1:26 The Bets Only He Would Sign\n3:41 Built Around One Man\n6:42 When the Accountant Takes the Wheel\n9:06 Who Can Replace a Founder?\n11:49 Tuesday\n\nFigures as of 12 November 2026, from Nvidia's filings and reporting by CNBC and Bloomberg.",
